{%- comment -%}
  Icon button: an icon-only button with a proper accessible name and a
  minimum 44x44px target.
  WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value, 2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum), 1.4.11 Non-text Contrast

  Usage (capture your theme's icon first, since render can't take a
  snippet name from a variable):
    {%- capture cart_icon -%}{% render 'icon-cart' %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {% render 'icon-button', label: 'Open cart', icon: cart_icon %}

  Accepts:
  - label: accessible name, required (e.g. 'Open search')
  - icon: the icon's SVG markup (captured, as above)
  - class: extra classes (optional)
  - attributes: extra HTML attributes as a string (optional)

  The icon is hidden from assistive technology so it is not announced twice.
{%- endcomment -%}

<button
  type="button"
  class="a11y-icon-button {{ class }}"
  aria-label="{{ label | escape }}"
  {{ attributes }}
>
  <span class="a11y-icon-button__icon" aria-hidden="true">
    {{- icon -}}
  </span>
</button>

<style>
  .a11y-icon-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-width: 44px;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0;
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .a11y-icon-button svg {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .a11y-icon-button:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
